1
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,920
Just know it lightly,
then step away, why don't you

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,620
Like someone is calling out to us,
the afternoon after the rain

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
led along by Mom's hand

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,420
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then

5
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:47,700
So, on the arcade guide tiles

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black parts

7
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:01,740
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

8
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,080
Stern-faced politicians,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too

9
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Turn that corner over there, why don't you

10
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone

11
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari
(there's a turtle there)

12
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:33,060
Everyone, come on over to our town

13
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you

14
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:46,060
This face.

15
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:48,140
There aren't any decent ones, are there.

16
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:51,820
Around this age, people don't want
to be photographed with their family,

17
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:54,680
right? Boys are like that.

18
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,540
This one.

19
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:58,280
It's a clipping

20
00:01:58,720 --> 00:01:59,720
This is the senior officer, isn't it?

21
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,360
And the girl beside him is a foreigner.

22
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:05,320
Ryo-chan's so nervous, it's adorable.

23
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,880
What on earth is this?

24
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,520
This one.

25
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,220
What was her name again, this girl?

26
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:15,040
Hey, Kankichi,
what was her name again, this girl?

27
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:17,640
This photo.

28
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:21,440
This is the girl I met when
I was delivering newspapers.

29
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,860
Newspaper delivery?

30
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:23,960
Ryo-chan did?

31
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:24,340
Yeah.

32
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:25,620
Really?

33
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,480
I can't believe it.

34
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,600
Why would you say that?

35
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,500
Because our senior is the type
who makes money the easy way.

36
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:36,280
Newspaper delivery, getting up early and going door to door one by one,
doing it the honest way?

37
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,120
Hey,

38
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:40,220
sorry I didn't do it the honest way, okay?

39
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:41,680
So how did you get started,

40
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:43,660
my best friend was doing it,

41
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:46,920
and I was recruited while
tagging along with him.

42
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:48,860
Yeah, yeah.

43
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:52,380
Um, what was her name again?

44
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,320
It's Tsuyoshi.

45
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,340
Right, right, Tsuyoshi-kun, Tsuyoshi-kun.

46
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:05,820
Hey, Kankushi! You again!
Go stand in the hallway!

47
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:07,440
Yes, sir.

48
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:14,761
Whenever I was made to stand in the hallway,

49
00:03:14,811 --> 00:03:17,000
there was always one guy I ran into.

50
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:19,340
That was Tsuyoshi Kanamoto.

51
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:22,300
He seemed cocky, and I didn't like him.

52
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:25,400
He always seemed to be
an outsider at school too.

53
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:28,138
Naturally, or inevitably,

54
00:03:28,188 --> 00:03:30,460
one day we finally got into a fight.

55
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:32,920
Damn it!

56
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:36,960
It wasn't like some youth drama, but after
we beat each other up, we became best friends.

57
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:41,300
We teamed up and got
into fights all the time.

58
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,240
We won every single fight.

59
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,540
What's with that face?

60
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:48,140
You! Remember this name!

61
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:50,780
Well, every now and then we lost too.

62
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,840
Tsuyoshi's father had died
of illness the previous year,

63
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:05,360
leaving Tsuyoshi to look after
his younger brother and sister.

64
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:07,480
So Mom went out to work.

65
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,020
That's why Tsuyoshi also,
to help with the household finances,

66
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,720
took up newspaper delivery.

67
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:19,460
Geez, don't nag me about this.

68
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,120
Apparently he's starting
newspaper delivery today.

69
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:27,460
There's no way that guy can get up early.

70
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:28,840
I'm off!

71
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:32,320
Before he starts the newspaper route,

72
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:35,780
he has to slip an advertising flyer
between the pages of each paper.

73
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:36,700
That's our job.

74
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,840
There are so many of them,
and it's really tough.

75
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:43,160
So then,

76
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:46,900
newspapers

77
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:48,400
newspapers

78
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:49,600
newspapers

79
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:52,958
I had about sixty houses on my route.

80
00:04:53,008 --> 00:04:56,880
If I forgot to deliver one,
it came out of my pay, so I was desperate.

81
00:04:59,020 --> 00:04:59,840
Welcome home.

82
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:03,440
This kid eats so much in the morning.
That's his fifth bowl.

83
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:06,820
Well, what do you expect?
I've been working since morning.

84
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:09,540
Geez, the food bills are killing us.

85
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:10,860
What's wrong with that?

86
00:05:10,910 --> 00:05:14,160
They say a house with a hardworking young
boy will soon be the talk of the neighborhood.

87
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:18,124
Well, with a son to be proud of,
both Dad and Mom,

88
00:05:18,174 --> 00:05:19,440
well, no wonder, right?

89
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:22,600
I wonder who he takes after.

90
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:28,380
Speaking of which,
when I was passing a shrine on my route,

91
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:31,100
I came across a pile of dirty
magazines someone had dumped there.

92
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:35,380
I picked up every one, stuffed them
between the newspapers, and took them home.

93
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:39,180
I was zooming along,
my heart pounding with excitement,

94
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,220
Are you all right?

95
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:44,760
It's serious.

96
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:48,340
Patrol cars are coming, ambulances
are coming, it's a huge commotion.

97
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:51,080
But if they find the porn mags on us,

98
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,440
we'll be taken in for questioning, I bet.

99
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,980
Desperately hiding the
scattered porn mags...

100
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:57,640
You, get in the ambulance quickly.

101
00:05:58,940 --> 00:05:59,660
I'm fine.

102
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,580
I have work, so I'll be going.

103
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:04,160
But blood is coming out of your head!

104
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:05,600
This one?

105
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,400
This has been coming out for a while.

106
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,620
I have a lot of tiny blood vessels,
so it comes out easily.

107
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:10,780
It's a personal injury accident, right?

108
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:12,100
But the victim...

109
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:13,140
I'm fine.

110
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:15,080
See, I'm perfectly fine.

111
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,200
Well, time for a quick run.

112
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,520
That kid's amazing

113
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:22,340
The truck was doing a good 70 kilometers an hour,
you know.

114
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,420
At least the porn mags didn't get found out.

115
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:27,220
My right hand was broken and my ribs were cracked,
you see.

116
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:30,540
I wrecked the bike,
so the old man's going to chew me out.

117
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,520
I was practically dying
until I got a 40-degree fever.

118
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,880
Still, I did deliver the
evening papers properly.

119
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,700
Like a pro, or whatever you'd call it.

120
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,840
I was even put in charge
of collecting the payments.

121
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:42,820
Quite a few houses had nobody home.

122
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,160
Dogs got sicced on me,
so it was really tough.

123
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:48,300
But my collection rate was 100%.

124
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,300
You're amazing when money's involved.

125
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,260
Because I'd stake out their
houses until I collected.

126
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:54,720
You're like a detective.

127
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:58,660
It even got me sent to the
hardest districts to collect from.

128
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:01,620
There was this guy who saved up a lot of money for a year,
then moved away.

129
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:03,780
Of course you went after him, right?

130
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:08,100
But since I was a grade schooler,
they totally looked down on me.

131
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:10,520
He had no intention of paying at all.

132
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,980
So pay me a year's worth of money!

133
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,280
What's with this brat?

134
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,880
I'll pay, I'll pay, I'll pay right now!

135
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:26,620
I'll have a scary-looking uncle I know come over,
you know.

136
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:27,560
Thanks for your continued business.

137
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,520
Just like you, Ryo-chan.

138
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:35,300
Back then, everyone was talking about a university
student girl from another delivery station.

139
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:39,180
I talked to that girl yesterday, you know.

140
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:40,360
Hey, is that true?

141
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:40,820
Hey.

142
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:42,160
What did you talk about?

143
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:47,100
I said, "Hello," and she said, "Hello."

144
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:50,280
Then I said, "Goodbye,
" and she said, "Goodbye."

145
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,340
That's all?

146
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:52,680
Yeah.

147
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,520
Idiot, I've talked to her like that too!

148
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:57,500
That doesn't count as talking!

149
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:58,180
Exactly.

150
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:00,360
Tch, I'm jealous as hell.

151
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,020
Then one day...

152
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,920
I once took shelter from a sudden shower,
you know.

153
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,360
I ended up sharing it with the
lady everyone was talking about.

154
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:22,740
Hello.

155
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:24,500
Hello.

156
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,560
We always pass each other, don't we?

157
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:27,120
Yes.

158
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,300
Are you in elementary school?

159
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:29,420
I'm in fifth grade.

160
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,180
You're always zooming
past at such great speed.

161
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:34,020
My route covers a lot of ground, so...

162
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:36,320
You work so hard every day.
That's admirable.

163
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:38,680
No, not at all.

164
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:41,820
Here you go.

165
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:45,040
Ah, thank you. I love chocolate.

166
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:49,426
It's made for adults,
so it might be a little bitter, but...

167
00:08:49,476 --> 00:08:51,580
The rain just won't stop, will it?

168
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:52,400
No, it won't.

169
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:02,660
At that moment,
I was hoping the rain would never stop.

170
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,780
It stopped raining. That's good.

171
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:11,320
Yes.

172
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,420
Just one more push, then.

173
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:16,580
Well then.

174
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:17,620
Well.

175
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,460
The chocolate was a little bitter,
after all.

176
00:09:28,340 --> 00:09:29,920
So you have some good memories too.

177
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:31,600
After that, with that person...

178
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:35,020
by the following March,
she'd been replaced by someone else.

179
00:09:35,020 --> 00:09:39,080
I don't know if she graduated
and went back home or got a job.

180
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,260
Meeting people is like that, isn't it.

181
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:44,680
Ryo-chan, what happened to that blonde girl?

182
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:45,860
Right.

183
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:51,420
There was an incredibly rich house on my delivery route,
you see.

184
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:14,080
Aaaaaah!

185
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:17,180
Okay, then who will solve this problem?

186
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:22,640
Kankichi!

187
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,580
If you're going to stand in the hallway,

188
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,600
Heh.

189
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,340
What's wrong?

190
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:50,660
Kae-chan...

191
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:56,000
collapsed.

192
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:01,240
She's under a lot of strain.

193
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:03,420
You shouldn't push yourself too hard, but

194
00:11:03,910 --> 00:11:05,640
please rest for the time being.

195
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:06,240
Yes.

196
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:17,220
Well then,

197
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,140
Hey, Tsuyoshi.

198
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:32,000
Hello, Uncle.

199
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:38,080
So, Tsuyoshi,

200
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:40,680
I've talked with your mom too, but

201
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:45,540
honestly, we can't keep going like this.
You understand that too, right?

202
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:46,280
Yes.

203
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:50,500
So, Uncle, how about you deliver newspapers for us?
What do you think?

204
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,240
Don't hold back.

205
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:54,980
Grandpa and Grandma
want to see you two, too.

206
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:56,140
Tsuyoshi.

207
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:07,320
That day, Tsuyoshi unusually came
along on my collection rounds.

208
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,240
Tsuyoshi, what are we doing after this?

209
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:10,860
Yeah, well...

210
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,700
Help! Help!

211
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:17,020
Please help me.

212
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:20,600
This way!

213
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,100
Exc-excuse me... I'm intruding!

214
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:28,320
Sorry!

215
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,120
Goodbye!

216
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:45,500
I've never run this much before.

217
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,280
Me too, me too.

218
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,920
Thanks for helping me.

219
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:57,460
Nice to meet you.

220
00:12:58,760 --> 00:12:59,860
The name's Tsuyoshi.

221
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,640
I'm Kankichi.

222
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:08,340
By the way, why are you being chased?

223
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:09,580
Who are those guys?

224
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:11,420
Well, you see...

225
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,300
Bodyguards.

226
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:18,800
I wasn't allowed outside,
so I stayed inside the house the whole time.

227
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,020
Every day.

228
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,760
So I ran away.

229
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:26,100
But your family must be worried.

230
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:29,153
Papa and Mama are both at work.

231
00:13:29,203 --> 00:13:31,020
I'm always alone at home.

232
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:33,546
Alright, in that case,

233
00:13:33,596 --> 00:13:36,040
leave it to us. Right, Tsuyoshi?

234
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:37,560
Yeah, that's right.

235
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:40,220
We'll keep you company for the whole day.

236
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:42,300
Really?

237
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:45,500
Don't hold back.

238
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:48,080
Thanks, Gan-kichi, Tsuyoshi.

239
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:55,160
So you live in that Western-style
mansion with the Doberman?

240
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:57,220
My house?

241
00:13:57,220 --> 00:13:59,140
Since I do newspaper deliveries,

242
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:01,880
The one who always speeds like crazy

243
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:02,620
You know about that?

244
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:06,600
But the other day he was going too fast, got hit by
a dump truck, and scattered porn magazines everywhere.

245
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,600
Porn magazines?

246
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,740
Idiot, don't say weird things!

247
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:15,240
Go on!

248
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,180
That's it, that's it!

249
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:28,760
Shut up, don't laugh!

250
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:39,100
Did you have fun, Flora?

251
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:42,320
This is the best.
I want to stay like this forever.

252
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,960
Should we just run off somewhere far away,
the three of us?

253
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,860
Welly? Suyoshi?

254
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,680
I'm joking, just joking.

255
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:59,638
Milady, where have you been?

256
00:14:59,688 --> 00:15:01,820
This old man was worried sick.

257
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,380
I'm fine. See, I'm perfectly safe.

258
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:06,260
By the way, who are these two?

259
00:15:07,887 --> 00:15:11,780
these gentlemen helped me when I got lost.

260
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:15,980
They even treated me to a meal
and walked me all the way home.

261
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:19,600
My young mistress is very
grateful for your help.

262
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:22,480
No, it was nothing that special.

263
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:24,214
I know!

264
00:15:24,264 --> 00:15:28,500
As a thank-you, I'd like to invite you
two to a garden party next Wednesday.

265
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:29,500
That's fine, isn't it?

266
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:32,780
Of course, if the young miss says so.

267
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:36,890
Buuurn, now that you mention a party,

268
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:39,540
I wonder if they'll
serve some awesome feast?

269
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,060
Well, why wouldn't they?

270
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:43,540
Yahoo, buuurn!

271
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,920
Idiot!

272
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,080
Sorry.

273
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:51,600
Who goes around playing on the way to work?

274
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:55,880
If you keep this up, people will think you ran off with the money,
and you won't be able to explain yourself.

275
00:15:56,420 --> 00:15:56,760
Yes.

276
00:15:57,220 --> 00:15:57,800
But...

277
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,440
I wanted to talk about something...

278
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:08,480
I see, so you're going back home.

279
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:09,200
Yes.

280
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:14,040
Your family's been through a lot, hasn't it.

281
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:16,980
Well, once you get there, work hard.

282
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:17,600
Yes.

283
00:16:18,340 --> 00:16:20,360
Well, I'll go deliver up to today's quota.

284
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:29,800
Hey, Tsuyoshi, I wonder if the party
will actually involve dancing and stuff.

285
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:31,420
I wonder.

286
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:32,840
I don't know what to do.

287
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:34,940
I can't dance or anything like that.

288
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:35,920
Hey, Tsuyoshi.

289
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,100
Shut up.

290
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,657
Party, party, party, you keep saying.

291
00:16:40,707 --> 00:16:43,400
There's no way I can go to a
place where I'd be so out of place.

292
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:47,460
A glamorous place like
a party doesn't suit me.

293
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:49,280
But if we don't go, Flora will...

294
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:53,580
Then go by yourself. I'm not going.

295
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:57,280
Tsuyoshi, what's gotten into
you all of a sudden, Tsuyoshi?

296
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,040
Shut up. What's your problem,

297
00:16:59,090 --> 00:17:02,840
you've been acting like an idiot the whole time.
Ugh, how embarrassing.

298
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:05,740
What, are you really going to
trample on Flora's feelings like that?

299
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:10,500
I'm not about to humor
some rich girl's whims.

300
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:14,340
And I don't want the
likes of you going, either.

301
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:16,820
I already told you, I'm not going!

302
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:20,520
Well, looks like we're through, then.

303
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:22,680
I'm done with you! We're through!

304
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:23,840
Fine by me.

305
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:24,460
See ya.

306
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:26,040
Why?

307
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:28,240
Tsuyoshi, you dumbass!

308
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:30,840
Go have your fun, then.

309
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:32,060
You idiot!

310
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:39,640
From the next day,
Tsuyoshi was gone from the delivery office.

311
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:42,180
Apparently Tsuyoshi quit.

312
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:44,240
Is that really true?

313
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,100
Yeah, he's apparently going
back to his home country.

314
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:49,160
His train leaves Ueno at
4 o'clock next Wednesday.

315
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,800
Anyone who wants to see
him off can leave early.

316
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:55,780
Garden party

317
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,660
It's kind of funny, isn't it?

318
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,580
Mom, this shirt's collar is choking me.

319
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:02,840
What are you talking about?

320
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:05,820
If you look ridiculous,
people will laugh at you, won't they, Dad?

321
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:06,940
Well, yeah.

322
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:10,940
A blue-eyed girlfriend, though?
Well done, Kankichi!

323
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:12,980
The Ryotsu family has gone international.

324
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:16,420
Well, someday I might even
have an international marriage.

325
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:19,680
What are you saying?
This guy's getting way ahead of himself.

326
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,120
Don't say such self-serving things.

327
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:25,700
But Tsuyoshi-kun, that's too bad.
He's moving today, isn't he?

328
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:27,480
It's fine. Forget that guy.

329
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:29,100
That guy's awful.

330
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:32,300
He keeps picking fights,
telling me to go to the party alone.

331
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:35,280
And he never told me a thing about moving.

332
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,280
That guy doesn't matter to me either.

333
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:39,060
That's not right, is it?

334
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:43,660
Kankichi, maybe Tsuyoshi-kun
found it hard to say goodbye to you.

335
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,880
Maybe he was just embarrassed.

336
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:51,620
But that guy, you know, he's basically...

337
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:54,220
If I'd known Tsuyoshi-kun
was moving today...

338
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:55,960
Would I go to a party with Ugiku?

339
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:58,780
If you don't go either, then...

340
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:00,660
That girl who's been looking
forward to it so much...

341
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:01,500
She'll be sad, won't she?

342
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:05,960
I didn't mention the stomach thing, and
I deliberately said things to pick a fight.

343
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,420
You're going to make her cry.

344
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:11,920
Got it, Kankichi.

345
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:14,340
Go and enjoy the party,
for Tsuyoshi-kun's sake too.

346
00:19:14,780 --> 00:19:17,600
If you make that girl cry,
Mom won't let you off easy.

347
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,181
To-day,

348
00:19:21,231 --> 00:19:26,520
Thank you for inviting me today.

349
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:27,500
This is for you.

350
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:29,480
Thanks, Kankichi.

351
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,300
What beautiful flowers.

352
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,280
Where's Tsuyoshi?

353
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:38,440
Th-that guy, he something urgent
came up and he couldn't make it.

354
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:40,700
I see, that's a shame.

355
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:43,980
Alright, let's go, Tsuyoshi.

356
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:45,160
Yeah.

357
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:15,480
Your hands will be free, won't they?

358
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:23,120
If you could support
someone with those hands.

359
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:29,740
How wonderful that would be.

360
00:20:29,740 --> 00:20:32,760
Dankichi-dick, won't you dance with me?

361
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:36,720
It's the thought, it's the thought.

362
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,220
It's all good, properly.

363
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,380
Sorry, Flora.

364
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:43,020
Kankichi!

365
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:49,540
I'm borrowing the Luger!

366
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:51,860
Come on, Kankichi!

367
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,280
How long?

368
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:35,000
Well, let's see.

369
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:35,980
About half an hour?

370
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:38,020
Maybe a little longer.

371
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,320
Tsuyoshi!

372
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:47,000
Kankichi!

373
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,600
Tsuyoshi!

374
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:52,140
Take care! Tsuyoshi!

375
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:55,860
You too! Kankichi!

376
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:01,380
Kankichi!

377
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:03,640
Tsuyoshi!

378
00:22:22,220 --> 00:22:25,400
This is Flora.

379
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:37,000
My happiest memory of Japan is

380
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:40,840
becoming friends with the two boys.

381
00:22:41,340 --> 00:22:45,900
They were both kind and gentle,
little gentlemen.

382
00:22:46,780 --> 00:22:50,120
I will never forget them.

383
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:55,400
Kankichi, Tsuyoshi, thank you.

384
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:01,880
Well, that's how it is.

385
00:23:02,340 --> 00:23:04,500
What a lovely memory.

386
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:07,660
Is that so? So this girl is Princess Flora?

387
00:23:07,660 --> 00:23:11,100
Yes, she was a beauty.
She could have been an actress.

388
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:14,600
If it's Princess Flora,
I've met her a few times.

389
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:15,380
Really?

390
00:23:16,020 --> 00:23:19,720
Yeah. I should have a photo
we took together recently.

391
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:20,220
What?

392
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:23,740
Look, the one next to me is Princess Flora.

393
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:25,280
Whoa!?

394
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:28,560
W-w-what, this is that girl!?

395
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:30,160
No way! That can't be!

396
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:32,680
No, there's no mistake about it.

397
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:34,540
No! Absolutely not!

398
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:37,900
It is her, I'm telling you!
I won't accept it!

399
00:23:37,940 --> 00:23:40,160
She's really put on a lot of weight,
hasn't she.

400
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:44,100
Doesn't she look kind and lovely?
She's aged gracefully.

401
00:23:44,100 --> 00:23:46,060
No! Absolutely not!

402
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:49,880
It's her!
Shall I call and confirm it, if you like!

403
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:52,820
No, it's not! Even if she herself admits it,

404
00:23:52,820 --> 00:23:56,520
I absolutely, absolutely,
absolutely won't accept it!

405
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:05,500
Kicking the alarm clock,
I stub my little toe, ouch ouch

406
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:13,920
Just drawing my eyebrows,
then dash, dash, dash to the station

407
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:19,620
Packed train,
surely dozing off against an old man's back

408
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:25,820
Another tough week, and the unreasonable
demands are, well, fair enough

409
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:33,340
Baguette in hand, playing it cool,
but it's a beef bowl with extra cloudy broth

410
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:40,220
Overtime-driven irritation,
cleared up neatly with more irritation

411
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:50,000
Every day's no problem,
once I've passed through a hot shower

412
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:56,560
Every day's no problem,
recharging my energy with a mesh pillow

413
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:06,180
Every day's no problem,
I love a girl like me

414
00:25:06,660 --> 00:25:13,000
Every day's no brain,
hearts flying on Monday

415
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:17,400
Mandeck, mandeck, no brain

416
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:22,360
It's a crow! A crow did it!

417
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:26,940
Damn it! A crow did it, so why do
I have to be the one under suspicion?

418
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:31,740
Wait! Even if it's my own screw-up,
if I just blame it on the crow!

419
00:25:31,740 --> 00:25:37,200
Next time, a huge clash!
Ryotsu versus the crow! See you then!

